Third-party material in tests/fixtures/

The files under tests/fixtures/ are short excerpts of pages, scripts and API responses that the named
companies serve publicly (the product is in each file name; each fixture's .json sidecar records the source
URL and the sha256 of the full body it was cut from). They are included only as test inputs, to show that
the extractors read what is really in those files. They are not covered by this repository's MIT license;
copyright stays with their owners. Values the engine redacts (keys, customer and organisation ids,
customer-named gates) have been replaced with placeholders of the same shape.

A company that wants a fixture of its material removed can ask through the exclusion issue template
(.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/exclusion.yml); it is removed, and the product is excluded from future runs.

docs/examples/ holds briefs written from public pages of Linear and Vercel on the dates they carry; the
quoted strings are those companies' and are quoted for commentary.
